# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CATENA — environment variables for NON-Wrangler hosts (Vercel / Netlify / CI)
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# This file mirrors `.dev.vars.example` key-for-key. The split is about WHO
# READS THE FILE, not about which keys exist:
#
#   .dev.vars   → read by `wrangler pages dev` and injected as `c.env`.
#                 Use this for local Cloudflare development.
#   .env        → read by generic Node tooling / CI, and the shape you paste
#                 into a host's environment UI (Vercel, Netlify, Render…).
#
# ⚠ WHICH TARGET ACTUALLY READS THESE  (corrected)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are SERVER-SIDE secrets consumed by the Hono app in src/api/index.ts.
# They take effect on every target that EXECUTES that app:
#
#   ✅ Cloudflare Pages   (`npm run build` → dist/_worker.js)   — reads c.env
#   ✅ `wrangler pages dev`                                      — reads .dev.vars
#   ✅ Vercel             (api/[[...route]].ts Edge Function)    — reads process.env
#        ↳ This is NEW. The Vercel target used to be pure static
#          (`outputDirectory: dist-static` and nothing else), so NOTHING executed
#          server-side and every key here was read by nobody — setting one in the
#          Vercel dashboard changed literally nothing, and every keyed panel was
#          permanently stuck on its deterministic fallback. `api/[[...route]].ts`
#          now mounts the same Hono app as an Edge Function alongside the static
#          output, so these keys finally do what this file always claimed.
#   ❌ Pure static hosts  (GitHub Pages, S3, `npm run serve:static`) — no server
#          exists, so nothing reads them. There the dashboard runs the in-browser
#          local engine, which deliberately receives NO secrets (a browser cannot
#          hold one). Only OPENAI_BASE_URL — a non-secret URL — may be exposed,
#          via `window.CATENA_PUBLIC_ENV`; see src/local/engine.ts → publicVars().
#
# NEVER inline any *_API_KEY or *_KEY below into client-side JS, an HTML
# <script>, or window.CATENA_PUBLIC_ENV. Anything the browser can read, every
# visitor can read. Keys belong to the server only. `npm run build:static` fails
# the build if it finds a secret-shaped literal in the artifact.
#
# Every value is OPTIONAL — see .dev.vars.example for exactly what each one
# upgrades and what the labelled fallback is. With this file absent the dashboard
# is still fully functional: 5 upstreams are live with no key at all.


# ── Nutrition ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-key-signup  (free, instant)
# Do not use the literal DEMO_KEY — globally rate-limited, returns HTTP 429.
USDA_API_KEY=

# ── LLM providers (any ONE enables live swarm/cascade inference) ─────────────
GROQ_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Non-secret. Defaults to https://www.genspark.ai/api/llm_proxy/v1 when unset.
OPENAI_BASE_URL=

# ── Supabase persistence (optional; twin is computed without it) ─────────────
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CLIENT-SIDE (non-secret) CONFIGURATION
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Not read from this file — listed here so every knob is documented in one place.
# Point the dashboard at an already-deployed Catena worker instead of running the
# API in-browser. Highest priority first:
#
#   1. ?api=https://your-project.pages.dev/api   URL param; persisted to
#                                                localStorage for later visits
#   2. <meta name="catena-api-base" content="…"> in public/dashboard.html
#   3. window.CATENA_API_BASE = "…"              set before core.js runs
#   4. localStorage["catena-api-base"]
#   5. <origin>/api                              same-origin — now satisfied by
#                                                Cloudflare Pages AND Vercel
#   6. in-browser local engine                   last resort, always available
#
# Each candidate is probed against `<base>/health` and must return
# `{"app":"catena"}` — a static host's 200-with-HTML SPA fallback can never be
# mistaken for a live API.
#
# To clear a remembered override:  localStorage.removeItem("catena-api-base")
# or visit the dashboard with ?api=  (empty value resets to same-origin).
